module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.BigSite.AffineOpensCech
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.BigSite.CrystalDeRhamPairs
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.BigSite.CrystalValuesProjective
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.Differentials.DeRhamPairZeroIdealLocalization

/-!
# The columns of the Čech–de Rham double complex over a base with zero divided power ideal

Fix a global crystalline situation `(p, (S, I, γ), X)` with `S` affine, write
`R = Γ(S, 𝒪_S)`, and let `N` be a crystal in finite locally free modules on `CRIS(X/S)`.  For an
affine open `V` of `X` the trivial thickening `(V, V, 0)` of [Stacks, Tag 07I8] is an object of
`AffineCris S` (`Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.trivialThickeningFunctor`), and

`V ↦ N(V, V, 0) ⊗_{Γ(V, 𝒪_V)} Ω^a_{Γ(V, 𝒪_V)/R, 0}`

with the maps of de Rham terms `Crystalline.DeRhamPair.termMap` is a presheaf of `R`-modules on
the affine opens of `X` (`trivialColumnPresheaf N a`), the degree-`a` part of the presheaf of de
Rham complexes `...bigCrystalDeRhamPresheaf` along `trivialThickeningFunctor`.  Its Čech complex
along a finite affine cover `U` of `X` is the column of the Čech–de Rham double complex
`C^{r, a} = ∏_x N(U_x, U_x, 0) ⊗ Ω^a_{U_x}`.

When `X` is separated and proper over `S` and `R` is Noetherian
(`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Crystalline/BigSite/TrivialBaseCechColumnsFinite.lean`):

* the cohomology of that Čech complex is a finite `R`-module in every degree, and vanishes in
  degrees `≥ #ι` (`moduleFinite_homology_trivialColumnPresheaf`,
  `isZero_homology_trivialColumnPresheaf`);
* there is a `D` such that `trivialColumnPresheaf N a` vanishes for `a > D`
  (`exists_isZero_trivialColumnPresheaf`).

The divided power ideal of a trivial thickening `(V, V, 0)` is zero whatever the base, so no
hypothesis on the divided power ideal of `R` is needed; this is the column of the Čech–de Rham
double complex over a base with zero divided power ideal, where it computes crystalline
cohomology.

## The proof

The formula `W ↦ N(W, W, 0) ⊗ Ω^a_{Γ(W)/R}` makes sense on every open `W` of `X`, and defines a
presheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules `trivialColumnModule N a` through the identification
`Γ(X, W) = Γ(W, 𝒪_W)` (`Scheme.restrictFunctorΓ`).  Over the affine opens it is the column presheaf
read over `R` (`trivialColumnPresheafIso`).  It **localizes on the basic opens of the affine
opens** (`isLocalizing_trivialColumnModule`): for `D(g) ⊆ V`,

* `N(D(g), D(g), 0) = Γ(D(g)) ⊗_{Γ(V)} N(V, V, 0)` because `N` is a crystal in quasi-coherent
  modules (`...SmallSite.bijective_crysBaseChange_of_isQuasicoherentOnSite`), and
  `Γ(D(g)) = Γ(V)_g`;
* the divided power ideal of `(V, V, 0)` is zero, so `Ω_{Γ(V)/R, 0}` is the module of Kähler
  differentials `Ω_{Γ(V)/R}` (`Crystalline.DeRhamPair.dividedPowerDifferentialRelations_eq_bot`),
  which localizes
  (`KaehlerDifferential.isLocalizedModule_map`);
* exterior powers and tensor products of localizations are localizations.

Its sections over an affine open are finite modules, the crystal being finite locally free and
`Γ(V)` of finite type over `R`.  So by `...AffineOpens.moduleFinite_homology_presheafSections` and
`...AffineOpens.isZero_homology_presheafSections` its Čech cohomology along `U` is the cohomology
of the coherent module it generates, which is finite by [Stacks, Tag 02O6] and vanishes above the
size of the cover by [Stacks, Tag 01XI].  For the bound on `a`, a finite affine cover `W_j` of `X`
has `Ω_{Γ(W_j)/R}` generated by `d_j` elements, so the column vanishes on `W_j` above `d_j`; every
affine open `V` is covered by opens which are basic in `V` and in some `W_j`, so the column, which
localizes, vanishes on `V` above `max_j d_j`.

## Main definitions

* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.openTrivialThickening` — `W ↦ (W, W, 0)` on all opens.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.trivialColumnPresheaf` — the column presheaf.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.trivialColumnModule` — the column module on `X`.
* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.trivialColumnPresheafIso` — the column presheaf is the
  presheaf of sections of the column module over the affine opens.

## Main results

* `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.TrivialColumn.isLocalization_ringMap` — the ring of
  sections of `(D(g), D(g), 0)` is the localization away from `g` of that of `(V, V, 0)`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07I8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07I8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07N5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07N5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01XI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01XI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02O6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02O6)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry Opposite
open scoped TensorProduct

universe u

namespace Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation

open SmallSite

variable (T : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u})

/-! ### The trivial thickenings of all the opens of `X` -/

/-- **The trivial thickening `(W, W, 0)` of an open `W` of `X`**, as an object of `Cris(X/S)`:
the image under `free` of the open immersion `W ⟶ X`. -/
def openTrivialThickening : T.X.Opens ⥤ CrystallineThickening T :=
  ObjectProperty.lift _ (T.X.restrictFunctor ⋙ free T)
    fun W ↦ (inferInstance : IsOpenImmersion W.ι)

/-! ### The de Rham terms over an object of `Cris(X/S)` -/

namespace TrivialColumn

variable {T} (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (crystallineStructureSheaf T)) (a : ℕ)

/-- The degree-`a` de Rham term `N(A) ⊗_{Γ(A)} Ω^a_{Γ(A)/R, δ}` over an object `A` of
`Cris(X/S)`. -/
abbrev term (A : CrystallineThickening T) : Type u :=
  (restrictSheafOfModules N).val.obj (op A) ⊗[sectionsDPRing T A.obj]
    ⋀[sectionsDPRing T A.obj]^a
      (dividedPowerDifferentials (A := Γ(T.S.scheme, ⊤)) (sectionsDPRing T A.obj).dividedPowers)

/-- The restriction of sections of `N` along a morphism of `Cris(X/S)`, semilinear over the map
of the rings of sections. -/
def restrict {A B : CrystallineThickening T} (k : A ⟶ B) :
    (restrictSheafOfModules N).val.obj (op B) →ₛₗ[(sectionsDPRingMap k.hom).toRingHom]
      (restrictSheafOfModules N).val.obj (op A) where
  toFun := crysSiteRestrict (restrictSheafOfModules N) k
  map_add' := crysSiteRestrict_add (restrictSheafOfModules N) k
  map_smul' c s := crysSiteRestrict_smul (restrictSheafOfModules N) k c s

/-- The map of de Rham terms along a morphism of `Cris(X/S)`, `m ⊗ ω ↦ k^* m ⊗ Ω_k(ω)`. -/
def termRestrict {A B : CrystallineThickening T} (k : A ⟶ B) : term N a B →+ term N a A :=
  DeRhamPair.tensorMap (sectionsDPRingMap k.hom) (restrict N k)
    (DeRhamPair.formsMap (sectionsDPRingMap k.hom) (isDPMorphism_sectionsDPRingMap k.hom) a)

/-- `termRestrict` is `Crystalline.DeRhamPair.termMap`. -/
theorem termRestrict_eq_termMap {A B : CrystallineThickening T} (k : A ⟶ B) (x : term N a B) :
    termRestrict N a k x =
      DeRhamPair.termMap (sectionsDPRingMap k.hom) (isDPMorphism_sectionsDPRingMap k.hom)
        (restrict N k) a x :=
  rfl

/-- `termRestrict` is semilinear. -/
theorem termRestrict_smul {A B : CrystallineThickening T} (k : A ⟶ B)
    (b : sectionsDPRing T B.obj) (x : term N a B) :
    termRestrict N a k (b • x) = sectionsDPRingMap k.hom b • termRestrict N a k x :=
  DeRhamPair.tensorMap_smul _ _ _ b x

/-- `termRestrict` of an identity. -/
theorem termRestrict_id (A : CrystallineThickening T) (x : term N a A) :
    termRestrict N a (𝟙 A) x = x :=
  DeRhamPair.termMap_eq_self _ _ (fun _ ↦ rfl) _
    (fun m ↦ crysSiteRestrict_id (restrictSheafOfModules N) A m) a x

/-- `termRestrict` of a morphism equal to an identity. -/
theorem termRestrict_eq_self {A : CrystallineThickening T} (k : A ⟶ A) (hk : k = 𝟙 A)
    (x : term N a A) : termRestrict N a k x = x := by
  subst hk
  exact termRestrict_id N a A x

/-- `termRestrict` of a composite. -/
theorem termRestrict_comp {A B C : CrystallineThickening T} (k : A ⟶ B) (k' : B ⟶ C)
    (x : term N a C) :
    termRestrict N a (k ≫ k') x = termRestrict N a k (termRestrict N a k' x) :=
  DeRhamPair.termMap_comp_of_eq _ _ (restrict N k') _ _ _ _
    (fun b ↦ DFunLike.congr_fun (sectionsDPRingMap_comp k.hom k'.hom) b)
    (restrict N k) (restrict N (k ≫ k'))
    (fun m ↦ (crysSiteRestrict_comp (restrictSheafOfModules N) k k' m).symm) a x

/-- `termRestrict` of a morphism equal to a composite. -/
theorem termRestrict_comp_of_eq {A B C : CrystallineThickening T} (k : A ⟶ B) (k' : B ⟶ C)
    (k'' : A ⟶ C) (hk : k'' = k ≫ k') (x : term N a C) :
    termRestrict N a k'' x = termRestrict N a k (termRestrict N a k' x) := by
  subst hk
  exact termRestrict_comp N a k k' x

end TrivialColumn

open TrivialColumn

/-! ### The column presheaf on the affine opens -/

variable {T} in
/-- **The degree-`a` column presheaf** `V ↦ N(V, V, 0) ⊗_{Γ(V)} Ω^a_{Γ(V)/R, 0}` on the affine
opens of `X`, read over `R = Γ(S, 𝒪_S)`, with the maps of de Rham terms
`Crystalline.DeRhamPair.termMap` along the trivial thickenings of the inclusions. -/
def trivialColumnPresheaf (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (crystallineStructureSheaf T)) (a : ℕ) :
    (AffineOpens T.X)ᵒᵖ ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} Γ(T.S.scheme, ⊤) where
  obj V := restrictScalarsModuleCat Γ(T.S.scheme, ⊤)
    (sectionsDPRing T ((trivialThickeningFunctor T).obj V.unop).obj.obj)
    ((restrictSheafOfModules N).val.obj (op ((trivialThickeningFunctor T).obj V.unop).obj) ⊗[
      sectionsDPRing T ((trivialThickeningFunctor T).obj V.unop).obj.obj]
      ⋀[sectionsDPRing T ((trivialThickeningFunctor T).obj V.unop).obj.obj]^a
        (dividedPowerDifferentials (A := Γ(T.S.scheme, ⊤))
          (sectionsDPRing T ((trivialThickeningFunctor T).obj V.unop).obj.obj).dividedPowers))
  map {V W} k := ConcreteCategory.ofHom (C := ModuleCat Γ(T.S.scheme, ⊤))
    (DeRhamPair.termMap (sectionsDPRingMap ((trivialThickeningFunctor T).map k.unop).hom.hom)
      (isDPMorphism_sectionsDPRingMap ((trivialThickeningFunctor T).map k.unop).hom.hom)
      (crystalPairRestrict ((trivialThickeningFunctor T).map k.unop)) a)
  map_id V := by
    refine ConcreteCategory.hom_ext _ _ fun x ↦ ?_
    exact termRestrict_eq_self N a _
      (congrArg (fun k ↦ k.hom) ((trivialThickeningFunctor T).map_id V.unop)) x
  map_comp {V W Z} k k' := by
    refine ConcreteCategory.hom_ext _ _ fun x ↦ ?_
    exact termRestrict_comp_of_eq N a _ _ _
      (congrArg (fun k ↦ k.hom) ((trivialThickeningFunctor T).map_comp k'.unop k.unop)) x

/-! ### The column as a presheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules on all the opens of `X` -/

namespace TrivialColumn

variable {T} (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (crystallineStructureSheaf T)) (a : ℕ)

variable (T) in
/-- The identification `Γ(X, W) = Γ(W, 𝒪_W)` of the sections of `𝒪_X` over an open `W` with the
ring of sections of the trivial thickening `(W, W, 0)`, the component of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.restrictFunctorΓ`. -/
def sectionsHom (W : T.X.Opens) :
    ↑(T.X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W)) →+*
      (sectionsDPRing T ((openTrivialThickening T).obj W).obj : Type u) :=
  (T.X.restrictFunctorΓ.inv.app (op W)).hom

/-- `sectionsHom` commutes with restriction. -/
theorem sectionsDPRingMap_sectionsHom {W W' : T.X.Opens} (h : W' ≤ W)
    (r : ↑(T.X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W))) :
    sectionsDPRingMap ((openTrivialThickening T).map (homOfLE h)).hom (sectionsHom T W r) =
      sectionsHom T W' (T.X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op r) :=
  (ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (T.X.restrictFunctorΓ.inv.naturality (homOfLE h).op) r).symm

/-- The sections of the column over an open `W`, as a module over `Γ(X, W)` through
`sectionsHom`. -/
@[instance_reducible]
def termModule (W : T.X.Opens) :
    Module ↑(T.X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W)) (term N a ((openTrivialThickening T).obj W)) :=
  Module.compHom _ (sectionsHom T W)

/-- The column `W ↦ N(W, W, 0) ⊗ Ω^a_{Γ(W)/R, 0}` on the opens of `X`, as an abelian presheaf. -/
def termPresheaf : T.X.Opensᵒᵖ ⥤ AddCommGrpCat.{u} where
  obj W := AddCommGrpCat.of (term N a ((openTrivialThickening T).obj W.unop))
  map i := AddCommGrpCat.ofHom (termRestrict N a ((openTrivialThickening T).map i.unop))
  map_id W := by
    ext x
    exact termRestrict_eq_self N a _ ((openTrivialThickening T).map_id W.unop) x
  map_comp i j := by
    ext x
    exact termRestrict_comp_of_eq N a _ _ _ ((openTrivialThickening T).map_comp j.unop i.unop) x

end TrivialColumn

open TrivialColumn

variable {T} in
/-- **The degree-`a` column as a presheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules on all the opens of `X`**:
`W ↦ N(W, W, 0) ⊗_{Γ(W)} Ω^a_{Γ(W)/R, 0}`, a module over `Γ(X, W) = Γ(W, 𝒪_W)`. -/
def trivialColumnModule (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (crystallineStructureSheaf T)) (a : ℕ) :
    PresheafOfModules.{u} T.X.ringCatSheaf.obj :=
  letI (W : T.X.Opensᵒᵖ) : Module ↑(T.X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj W) ((termPresheaf N a).obj W) :=
    termModule N a W.unop
  PresheafOfModules.ofPresheaf (termPresheaf N a) fun {W _} i r x ↦
    (termRestrict_smul N a ((openTrivialThickening T).map i.unop) (sectionsHom T W.unop r) x).trans
      (congrArg (· • termRestrict N a ((openTrivialThickening T).map i.unop) x)
        (sectionsDPRingMap_sectionsHom (leOfHom i.unop) r))

/-- Two composites of restriction maps of `𝒪_X` with the same source and target agree. -/
theorem presheaf_map_map_eq {X : Scheme.{u}} {U₁ U₂ U₂' U₃ : X.Opens} (a : op U₁ ⟶ op U₂)
    (d : op U₂ ⟶ op U₃) (b : op U₁ ⟶ op U₂') (c : op U₂' ⟶ op U₃) (z : Γ(X, U₁)) :
    X.presheaf.map d (X.presheaf.map a z) = X.presheaf.map c (X.presheaf.map b z) := by
  rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp,
    ← Functor.map_comp]
  rfl

/-- The structure map of the trivial thickening of an open `W`, on global sections, is `f^♯`
followed by restriction and the identification `sectionsHom`. -/
theorem sectionsHom_baseHom (W : T.X.Opens) (r : Γ(T.S.scheme, ⊤)) :
    sectionsHom T W (T.X.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op ((sourceToBase T).appTop r)) =
      algebraMap Γ(T.S.scheme, ⊤) (sectionsDPRing T ((openTrivialThickening T).obj W).obj) r :=
  presheaf_map_map_eq (U₁ := ⊤) (U₂ := W) (U₃ := W.ι ''ᵁ ⊤)
    (U₂' := W.ι ''ᵁ W.ι ⁻¹ᵁ (sourceToBase T ⁻¹ᵁ ⊤)) _ _ _ _ _

variable {T} in
/-- **Over the affine opens, the column presheaf is the presheaf of sections of the column
module**, read over `R = Γ(S, 𝒪_S)`. -/
def trivialColumnPresheafIso (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (crystallineStructureSheaf T)) (a : ℕ) :
    trivialColumnPresheaf N a ≅
      AffineOpens.presheafSections (sourceToBase T) (trivialColumnModule N a) :=
  NatIso.ofComponents (fun V ↦ LinearEquiv.toModuleIso (R := Γ(T.S.scheme, ⊤))
    (X₁ := (trivialColumnPresheaf N a).obj V)
    (X₂ := (AffineOpens.presheafSections (sourceToBase T) (trivialColumnModule N a)).obj V)
    (g₁ := ModuleCat.isAddCommGroup _) (g₂ := ModuleCat.isAddCommGroup _)
    (m₁ := ModuleCat.isModule _) (m₂ := ModuleCat.isModule _)
    { toFun := fun x ↦ x
      invFun := fun x ↦ x
      left_inv := fun _ ↦ rfl
      right_inv := fun _ ↦ rfl
      map_add' := fun _ _ ↦ rfl
      map_smul' := fun r x ↦ by
        let y : term N a ((openTrivialThickening T).obj V.unop.obj) := x
        change algebraMap Γ(T.S.scheme, ⊤)
            (sectionsDPRing T ((openTrivialThickening T).obj V.unop.obj).obj) r • y =
          sectionsHom T V.unop.obj
            (T.X.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op ((sourceToBase T).appTop r)) • y
        rw [sectionsHom_baseHom] })
    fun _ ↦ rfl

/-! ### The column localizes on the basic opens of the affine opens -/

namespace TrivialColumn

variable {T} (N : SheafOfModules.{u} (crystallineStructureSheaf T)) (a : ℕ)

/-- **The divided power ideal of a trivial thickening is zero.** -/
theorem ideal_eq_bot (W : T.X.Opens) :
    (sectionsDPRing T ((openTrivialThickening T).obj W).obj).ideal = ⊥ :=
  SheafOfModules.Submodule.bot_obj _ _

/-- `sectionsHom` as a ring isomorphism. -/
def sectionsEquiv (W : T.X.Opens) :
    ↑(T.X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W)) ≃+*
      (sectionsDPRing T ((openTrivialThickening T).obj W).obj : Type u) :=
  (T.X.restrictFunctorΓ.app (op W)).symm.commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv

/-- `sectionsEquiv` is `sectionsHom`. -/
theorem sectionsEquiv_apply (W : T.X.Opens) (r : ↑(T.X.ringCatSheaf.obj.obj (op W))) :
    sectionsEquiv W r = sectionsHom T W r :=
  rfl

/-- The map of rings of sections of the trivial thickenings along an inclusion of opens. -/
abbrev ringMap {W V : T.X.Opens} (h : W ≤ V) :
    (sectionsDPRing T ((openTrivialThickening T).obj V).obj : Type u) →ₐ[Γ(T.S.scheme, ⊤)]
      sectionsDPRing T ((openTrivialThickening T).obj W).obj :=
  sectionsDPRingMap ((openTrivialThickening T).map (homOfLE h)).hom

/-- **The ring of sections of the trivial thickening of a basic open `D(g)` of an affine open `V`
is the localization away from `g` of that of `V`.** -/
theorem isLocalization_ringMap {V : T.X.Opens} (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (g : Γ(T.X, V)) :
    letI := DeRhamPair.algebraOf (ringMap (T.X.basicOpen_le g))
    IsLocalization.Away (sectionsHom T V g)
      (sectionsDPRing T ((openTrivialThickening T).obj (T.X.basicOpen g)).obj) := by
  let := DeRhamPair.algebraOf (ringMap (T.X.basicOpen_le g))
  have := hV.isLocalization_basicOpen g
  let : Algebra Γ(T.X, V)
      (sectionsDPRing T ((openTrivialThickening T).obj (T.X.basicOpen g)).obj) :=
    ((sectionsHom T (T.X.basicOpen g)).comp
      (T.X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (T.X.basicOpen_le g)).op).hom).toAlgebra
  let e : Γ(T.X, T.X.basicOpen g) ≃ₐ[Γ(T.X, V)]
      (sectionsDPRing T ((openTrivialThickening T).obj (T.X.basicOpen g)).obj : Type u) :=
    { sectionsEquiv (T.X.basicOpen g) with commutes' := fun _ ↦ rfl }
  have : IsLocalization (Submonoid.powers g)
      (sectionsDPRing T ((openTrivialThickening T).obj (T.X.basicOpen g)).obj) :=
    IsLocalization.isLocalization_of_algEquiv (Submonoid.powers g) e
  refine IsLocalization.of_ringEquiv_left (M₁ := Submonoid.powers g)
    (sectionsEquiv V).symm ?_ ?_
  · exact (Submonoid.map_powers _ _).trans
      (congrArg Submonoid.powers ((sectionsEquiv V).symm_apply_apply g))
  · intro x
    exact (congrArg (ringMap (T.X.basicOpen_le g))
      ((sectionsEquiv V).apply_symm_apply x).symm).trans
      (sectionsDPRingMap_sectionsHom (T.X.basicOpen_le g) ((sectionsEquiv V).symm x))

end TrivialColumn

end Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation
